            'Aces are always low.',
            'Straights and flushes are ignored for low ranking.',
            'Best hand is A-2-3-4-5 (wheel).',
            'Hands are compared from highest card downward among low hands.',
            'In some California rules, made sevens may be forced to bet.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prefer smooth lows and avoid drawing to rough one-card gutters.',
          intermediate: 'Use opponent draw counts to estimate made hands versus drawing hands.',
          advanced: 'Apply pressure when pat, and represent made lows in heads-up final betting spots.',
          tips: [
            'A-2-3 starts are strong; rough 9-low draws are often traps.',
            'A pat hand can be value or bluff depending on prior draw pattern.',
          ],
